D_SERVICE_MEDIA_PROJECTION, permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK) are already granted by default? I checked…"],["b9b85b6c_8096c3e0",21,-6,0,"narrowing the set to one primary type feels weird, especially if there are multiple capturing types."],["86d509dc_92f0356a",21,-2,1,"i recommend adding a comment here that the capturing cases are first explicitly and why."]],0,417],[7155787,20413,22,0.796,0.587,[[8,35]],[["5d6b3889_4ec76942",21,-7,1,"In current patchaet, we pass the global mediaTypes to here. I am thinking about a sequence. User opens screen sharing in 1st tab -> User opens camera in 2nd tab. The displayed notification is for 2nd…"],["c8ed3298_7611f606",21,-7,1,"The logic seems incorrect to me. We compare `global` mediaTypes with `local` mediaTypes of a tab. It makes the tab will always destroy and re-create when we have multiple media tabs even the `local`…"]],0,418],[7172080,20417,135,4.14,3.17,[[8,0.421,36,57],[37,0.372,10,53],[3,0.207,28,25]],[["757bcdf4_040db4b8",18,-5,0,"Super nit: `includable` to me means this returns `true` to include and `false` to exclude. Should this be `should_exclude_web_contents_filter`? Although maybe this is not the convention so feel free…"],["c4908be6_ab10f4bb",22,-5,0,"Optional: ```suggestion boolean shouldFilterWebContents( long nativeMediaCapturePickerManagerBridge, @JniType(\"content::WebContents*\") WebContents webContents); ``` You can also optionally do this…"]],0,419],[7202249,20417,8,0.421,0.3,[[3,0.727,29,6],[8,0.273,37,2]],[["44d8c4f8_53c9dbc4",22,0,0,"that's a neat trick."]],0,420],[7155472,20419,267,6.141,4.678,[[37,0.766,11,198],[8,0.234,38,59]],[["11a6e8f8_ea7fc9b7",23,-1,1,"Optional: ```suggestion final List<TabModelSelector> selectors = List.of(sTestRule.getSelector); ``` If the mutability of the list doesn't matter."]],0,421],[7206372,20419,166,4.14,3.17,[[8,0.77,39,125],[37,0.23,12,37]],[["176d7d7c_b5b25028",20,0,0,"Should we add the other update functions just to be safe?"],["26928151_5d6649c5",20,0